    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups for our speed-oriented assets. **Jackson Merrill** (73.24) earns the top spot in today\u2019s projection, buoyed by a prime matchup against Roki Sasaki; he benefits from a massive 100% stolen base opportunity rating against a slow-delivering pitcher, paired with a strong platoon advantage that pushes his efficiency score to an elite tier. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** (70.43) is an essential start despite his lower base projection. While his batting order slot is suboptimal, his matchup against Trevor Rogers\u2014combined with an 87% stolen base success rate against the pitcher's delivery\u2014makes him a critical catalyst for our league-leading pursuit of the SB category. **Kyle Tucker** (69.85) remains a staple, capitalizing on the high-upside environment of his current park, while **Josh Jung** (64.84) provides stability against the weak arm of Patrick Corbin.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was the exclusion of **Curtis Mead** (58.36), who narrowly missed the cut for the final utility spot. While **Mead** benefits from a high park factor and a favorable matchup against Trevor Rogers, the optimizer favored **Jacob Wilson** (60.11) for his slightly higher SP skill profile and projected role consistency. We also held **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.70) on the bench; despite his elite BvP history against Nathan Eovaldi, the combination of Eovaldi\u2019s high-caliber pitching and a negative platoon split made him a luxury we couldn't justify while prioritizing volume and category efficiency elsewhere.\n\nRisk management remains a primary concern as we await official confirmation for several slots. **Drake Baldwin** (54.83) currently sits at the bottom of our start threshold; should his lineup position drop, we are prepared to pivot to more secure options to protect our daily game caps. We are also closely monitoring the platoon dynamics for **Gunnar Henderson** (59.45); his score is constrained by an unfavorable lefty-lefty matchup against Andrew Alvarez. While **Henderson** remains in the lineup due to his high talent floor, he will need to overcome the 10% penalty associated with the pitcher\u2019s skill to provide value. All owners should maintain vigilance regarding weather alerts, though no immediate field-level risks are currently suppressing the aggregate efficiency of our starting lineup.",
